Worker in `src/photos/upload-queue.ts`:

```ts
const MAX_CONCURRENT = 3;
let active = 0;

export const drainQueue = async () => {
  while (active < MAX_CONCURRENT) {
    const next = await claimNextPending();
    if (!next) return;
    active++;
    void uploadOne(next).finally(() => {
      active--;
      void drainQueue();
    });
  }
};
```

`claimNextPending` flips one row from `pending` to `uploading` in a single UPDATE, so two loops can't grab the same photo. It runs after each capture and when connectivity returns, so queued photos go out once the app is back online.

