The server returns `fieldVersions: [{ inspectionId, field, value, wall, counter, nodeId }]`. New merge in `src/sync/merge.ts`:

```ts
export const mergeFieldVersions = async (db: Db, versions: FieldVersion[]) => {
  await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
    let clock = await loadHlc(tx);
    for (const v of versions) {
      const remote = { wall: v.wall, counter: v.counter, nodeId: v.nodeId };
      clock = receive(clock, remote, Date.now());
      const local = await getFieldClock(tx, v.inspectionId, v.field);
      if (local && compareHlc(local, remote) >= 0) continue;
      await applyRemoteField(tx, v, remote);
    }
    await saveHlc(tx, clock);
  });
};
```

Local dirty fields with a higher clock are kept, and the server will take them on the next push. Before this, the whole record was overwritten.

