Simpler and honest: a small token bucket, written by us, with the in-memory store.

```diff
--- a/src/ingestion/rate-limit.ts
+++ b/src/ingestion/rate-limit.ts
@@
-export const ingestRateLimit = {
-  max: 100,
-  timeWindow: "1 second",
-  keyGenerator: (req: FastifyRequest) => req.apiKeyPrefix,
-};
+export const INGEST_RATE_PER_SECOND = 300;
+export const INGEST_BURST = 600;
+
+type Bucket = { tokens: number; updatedAt: number };
+const buckets = new Map<string, Bucket>();
+
+export function takeToken(key: string, now = Date.now()): boolean {
+  const b = buckets.get(key) ?? { tokens: INGEST_BURST, updatedAt: now };
+  const refill = ((now - b.updatedAt) / 1000) * INGEST_RATE_PER_SECOND;
+  b.tokens = Math.min(INGEST_BURST, b.tokens + refill);
+  b.updatedAt = now;
+  const allowed = b.tokens >= 1;
+  if (allowed) b.tokens -= 1;
+  buckets.set(key, b);
+  return allowed;
+}
```

- limit goes from 100 to 300 requests per second, with a burst of 600, still keyed on the API key prefix
- the in-memory store lives in the process, so the limit applies per Fly machine
- with N machines the real ceiling for a tenant is up to N x 300/s
- I dropped @fastify/rate-limit for this route; the hook calls takeToken and returns 429 on false

Good catch, it grows by one entry per distinct key and never evicts. Key count is bounded by tenants, so it is small, but I'll add a sweep anyway.

