Problem: two parallel uploads hitting 401 would both call refresh, and the second replay trips reuse detection and logs the user out. Need a single in-flight promise.

```diff
+let inflight: Promise<void> | null = null;
+
+export function refreshSession(): Promise<void> {
+  inflight ??= doRefresh().finally(() => {
+    inflight = null;
+  });
+  return inflight;
+}
+
+async function doRefresh(): Promise<void> {
+  const refresh = await SecureStore.getItemAsync('refresh_token');
+  if (!refresh) throw new SessionExpiredError();
+  const res = await fetch(`${API}/auth/refresh`, {
+    method: 'POST',
+    headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
+    body: JSON.stringify({ refresh_token: refresh }),
+  });
+  if (res.status === 401) throw new SessionExpiredError();
+  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`refresh failed: ${res.status}`);
+  const pair = await res.json();
+  await SecureStore.setItemAsync('access_token', pair.access);
+  await SecureStore.setItemAsync('refresh_token', pair.refresh);
+}
```

- Network errors do not clear the session, so offline devices stay logged in.
- Only a 401 from `/auth/refresh` forces re-login.
- Also call `refreshSession()` in the AppState foreground handler before the immediate sync.

