- EAS Build picks the install command from the lockfile, so with `pnpm-lock.yaml` present and `package-lock.json` gone it runs `pnpm install`.
- `"corepack": true` makes the build worker activate the version from `packageManager`, so it uses `pnpm@10.11.0` instead of whatever the image ships.
- `NPM_CONFIG_LEGACY_PEER_DEPS` only existed to get past npm peer conflicts, so I removed it.
- `.npmrc` is committed, so the worker gets `node-linker=hoisted`. `GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN` is already an EAS secret from S21.
